note Exercism-style exercise "queen-attack": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/queen-attack
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note Rows and columns run 0 .. 7. create checks one queen's position: 0 valid, 1 row negative,
note 2 row past the board, 3 column negative, 4 column past the board (row checked first).
note canattack is true when queens at (wr, wc) and (br, bc) share a row, column or diagonal.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/queen-attack
om2
fn create row long col long to int
if lt row 0
ret 1
end
if gt row 7
ret 2
end
if lt col 0
ret 3
end
if gt col 7
ret 4
end
ret 0
end
fn canattack wr long wc long br long bc long to bool
dr = sub wr br
dc = sub wc bc
if lt dr 0
dr = neg dr
end
if lt dc 0
dc = neg dc
end
ret or or eq dr 0 eq dc 0 eq dr dc
end
